rOptions \\n```\\n**Extends:** RenderOptions\\n\\n\\n<table><thead><tr><th>\\n\\nProperty\\n\\n\\n</th><th>\\n\\nModifiers\\n\\n\\n</th><th>\\n\\nType\\n\\n\\n</th><th>\\n\\nDescription\\n\\n\\n</th></tr></thead>\\n<tbody><tr><td>\\n\\ncheckOrigin?\\n\\n\\n</td><td>\\n\\n\\n</td><td>\\n\\nboolean \\\\| 'lax-proto'\\n\\n\\n</td><td>\\n\\n_(Optional)_ Protection against cross-site request forgery (CSRF) attacks.\\n\\nWhen `true`<!-- -->, for every incoming POST, PUT, PATCH, or DELETE form submissions, the request origin is checked to match the server's origin. `lax-proto` is for SSL-terminating proxies\\n\\nBe careful when disabling this option as it may lead to CSRF attacks.\\n\\nDefaults to `true`<!-- -->.\\n\\n\\n</td></tr>\\n<tr><td>\\n\\nrender\\n\\n\\n</td><td>\\n\\n\\n</td><td>\\n\\nRender\\n\\n\\n</td><td>\\n\\n\\n</td></tr>\\n<tr><td>\\n\\ntrustForwardedHeaders?\\n\\n\\n</td><td>\\n\\n\\n</td><td>\\n\\nboolean\\n\\n\\n</td><td>\\n\\n_(Optional)_ Use the `X-Forwarded-Host` and `X-Forwarded-Proto` request headers to compute the URL exposed by `useLocation()` during SSR.\\n\\nOnly enable this when the server is behind a proxy that overwrites these headers, otherwise clients can spoof the URL.\\n\\nDefaults to `false`<!-- -->.\\n\\n\\n</td></tr>\\n</tbody></table>\",","       \"editUrl\": \"https://github.com/QwikDev/qwik/tree/main/packages/qwik-router/src/middleware/request-handler/types.ts\",","       \"mdFile\": \"router.serverrenderoptions.md\"","     },"],"additions":1,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/docs/src/routes/api/qwik-router-middleware-request-handler/index.mdx","lines":["@@ -1894,6 +1894,25 @@ Render"," "," </td><td>"," ","+</td></tr>","+<tr><td>","+","+trustForwardedHeaders?","+","+</td><td>","+","+</td><td>","+","+boolean","+","+</td><td>","+","+_(Optional)_ Use the `X-Forwarded-Host` and `X-Forwarded-Proto` request headers to compute the URL exposed by `useLocation()` during SSR.","+","+Only enable this when the server is behind